        "research_rationale": "EO 8637 is a one-person retirement exemption. Identity: the held text is the American Presidency Project page (node 368287, Common Crawl capture 2026-01-24T12:43:11Z); the page record with the same sha256 has a heading naming Executive Order 8637, the date 1941-01-14 that matches the signature date in the text, and a text_sha256 equal to the held file. The text was read in full: one recital paragraph, one operative sentence, signature and date. Inventory: a single clause, the exemption of Joshua G. Hefty. End: the stated period gives 1942-01-31 as the first end by the order's own terms. EO 8969, signed December 11, 1941, cites this order by number (\"Executive Order No. 8637 of \") and exempts the same employee again: \"I hereby further exempt\" ... \"for a period of one year ending January 31, 1943\". It states no separate effective date, so its signature date is recorded as the event date. It is a later event, not an end: it is a new exemption for a later period and does not revoke, shorten or supersede the exemption in EO 8637. The packet's machine searches (U.S. Code release point 119-121, eCFR as of 2026-10-14, OFR catalog, and held-text person-name search) record no hit that revokes, supersedes or shortens the order. The record rests on a transcription: original not yet held; replace and re-check quotes when an official copy is retrieved.\nMember checks: {\"earlier_end_check\":\"No earlier end found. The order fixes its own period ending 1942-01-31; the packet's U.S. Code, eCFR and OFR-catalog machine searches record no hit that ends it earlier. The only later order citing EO 8637 is EO 8969, an extension that does not revoke it. Nothing in the held evidence shows the exemption ended before January 31, 1942.\",\"independent_command_check\":\"The recital states the public-interest finding and the operative sentence is the only command; the signature and date add none. No independent command survives the stated end.\",\"savings_check\":\"Checked the order for a savings or continuing provision: none appears in the held text. The only surviving effect is the service already rendered under the exemption.\",\"scope_check\":\"One clause covering the whole order: the exemption of Joshua G. Hefty. The held text was read in full; it exempts one named employee for one period and covers no other person, position or period.\"}",
